      {
        "author": {
          "login": "LucioFranco"
        },
        "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
        "body": "> At one point when we talked about this, I thought you said that the solution was to just force the initial block_on to continue running the driver until all other block_ons finish, and then return that future's output — am i misremembering, or just wrong?\r\n\r\nNo, we wanted to actually move the driver between threads. I think that would be odd to have the block_on run longer than expected? That feels like an implicit dependency that would be pretty surprising.",
